{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540071-da-v-what-exactly-is-an-\u201cagent-of-virtue\u201d","id":1540071,"title":"DA: V. What exactly is an \u201cAgent of virtue\u201d?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-08T18:39:37-07:00","id":1540071,"title":"DA: V. What exactly is an \u201cAgent of virtue\u201d?","content":"As above.<br /> The Road of Sin\u2019s Hierarchy of Sin 1 is \u201cEncouraging virtue or aiding agents of virtue.\u201d<br /> What is an agent of virtue?<br /> Is it someone on the Road of Heaven? Humanity? Anybody espousing a code that puts others before the self?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T20:52:45-07:00","id":1540072,"title":"","content":"Just off the top of my head, anyone who through word or deed is encouraging others to practice such things as charity, temperance, justice, and other forms of good will, selflessness, and/or righteousness. <br /> However, it is possible that the Road of Sin book gave a more detailed description, but I don't have that book handy to check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T13:15:31-07:00","id":1540098,"title":"","content":"I'm going with people who try to make things better for others and in regards to Kindred I'm going with the ones who hold onto there humanity strongly or follow the Road of Heaven intently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T20:20:20-07:00","id":1540119,"title":"","content":"I agree with what was said. This could include vampires on the road of heaven or humanity, and it could certainly include mortal saints or just generally good people.<br /> <br /> As a personal aside, I would allow for the caveat that a vampire on the Road of Sin could work with someone like that, and even help or encourage them to a degree, provided ther Sinner's end goal was to corrupt the person or institution that was being aided. For example, helping a genuinely good person out for the express goal of eventually corrupting and/or betraying them, or helping someone set up a soup kitchen so you could corrupt the people there and turn it into your haven.<br /> <br /> I feel like tricking and betraying a saint by first encouraging and working with them is absolutely in the Road of Sin's wheelhouse. But helping good people and encouraging them to do good for the sake of good is <i>bad</i>, at least for the Road of Sin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T05:33:08-07:00","id":1540347,"title":"","content":"Many thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T18:10:19-07:00","id":1540539,"title":"","content":"The notion of an agent of virtue is problematic, due to its vague and undefined nature. I don't think <i>Road of Sin</i> defines this, though it is one of those books where it is hard to find that kind of information. I would presume that an agent of virtue is a person specifically encouraging virtue in a specific situation; being a good person is not enough, but being a priest trying to (for instance) encourage parishioners to renounce gluttony might be. And this is, of course, a secondary problem, in that we will get some interesting outcomes if we apply medieval notions of virtue and vice. Torturing someone you think has heretical beliefs to the point where they return to orthodoxy is fine and virtuous; failing to pray at an appointed time may be seen as a great vice and deserving of punishment...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T00:37:13-07:00","id":1540825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540071-da-v-what-exactly-is-an-\u201cagent-of-virtue\u201d?p=1540539#post1540539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The notion of an agent of virtue is problematic, due to its vague and undefined nature. I don't think <i>Road of Sin</i> defines this, though it is one of those books where it is hard to find that kind of information. I would presume that an agent of virtue is a person specifically encouraging virtue in a specific situation; being a good person is not enough, but being a priest trying to (for instance) encourage parishioners to renounce gluttony might be. And this is, of course, a secondary problem, in that we will get some interesting outcomes if we apply medieval notions of virtue and vice. Torturing someone you think has heretical beliefs to the point where they return to orthodoxy is fine and virtuous; failing to pray at an appointed time may be seen as a great vice and deserving of punishment...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}